  "releaseNotes": "## Highlights\n- **Exposures and conversions you can send anywhere.** Exposures (who saw which variant) and conversions (what they did next) flow through opt-in streams into batched, isolated sinks (), with drop counters for every stage.\n- **Metrics and traces out of the box.** A  meter ( by experiment, variant and outcome) and  events on the active trace, following the OpenTelemetry convention.\n- **A complete OpenFeature provider.** Lifecycle,  events, accurate resolution details (, , , , error messages, flag metadata), , and a new  package that builds the evaluation context once per request.\n- **Analysis-ready exposures.** Each exposure carries  (a fingerprint of the experiment's definition) and, per experiment, the context attributes listed under .\n- **Restructured documentation.** The README is a front page; the detail lives in topic pages under .\n\n## New\n- , , , and  for conversions, natively and through OpenFeature.\n- , ,  (with , , ).\n- : one notification per update with the ids that really changed.\n-  and ; .\n-  is public.\n-  is public; .\n-  ( in JSON and appsettings).\n\n## Breaking changes\n-  is now ; the sink pipeline is generic over the event type.\n-  and  are gone; use  and the  overloads.\n- OpenFeature reasons: hashed assignment is  (was ) and a wrong value type is  (was ).\n-  has new optional constructor arguments.\n- ,  and  have new members.\n\n## Fixes\n-  is now applied to every evaluation.\n- Exposure timestamps come from the registered .\n\n## Maintenance\n- Aspire samples and tests upgraded to 13.6.1, which no longer pulls the vulnerable  2.5.192.",
